{"id":41149784559809,"type":"album","name":"undun","artist":"The Roots","year":2011,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/2932-undun_093623.jpg","aoty":82,"aoty_user":88,"sputnik":4.09,"yt":"feKLrWAzmVM","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-roots/undun","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/2932-the-roots-undun.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/88825/The-Roots-undun/"},"desc":"Undun is the twelfth studio album by American hip hop band The Roots, released on December 2, 2011, by Def Jam Recordings. Recording sessions for the album took place at several recording locations in Philadelphia and New York City. Production was handled primarily by Questlove, record producer and drummer for the band. Undun incorporates neo soul and indie music elements. It is an existential concept album about the short, tragic life of fictional character Redford Stevens, set in urban poverty, and is told through a reverse-chronological narrative. The album performed modestly on music charts and sold 112,000 copies in the ."},"artist_ref":{"id":124965019676686,"name":"The Roots","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/2010efb36cdab69843bd26026b1c5ce2/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":26869950655266,"type":"genre","name":"Conscious Hip Hop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":252,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":39329334330192,"type":"genre","name":"East Coast Hip Hop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":251,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":16699661381161,"name":"RYM Top — Hip Hop — Conscious Hip Hop","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":45,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":45584128953585,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — East Coast Hip Hop","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":53,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":174195132705744,"name":"Sputnikmusi